-- skills (one marked `travel`, the path's travel power) and a super. New keys used below:
--   ride (shape)  a travel power: the hero rides at up to `speed` for `duration`; `ride` = "air" (free flight),
--                 "surf" (along streets, walls and water) or "rail" (a straight grind along the aim);
--                 `trail` coeff hurts what the ride passes
--   launch (shape) the hero springs `up` studs and `forward`; `recasts` = extra uses before the cooldown
--   place (shape) a point on the ground along the aim (decoys)
--   summon        the look of a field that strikes the nearest robot (`single`): turret, drone, clones...
--   form, scale   a transformation while the buff lasts; `extra` = more buffs { kind, value }
--   delay         the hit robot bursts `delay` s later for `delayCoeff` around it (`delayRadius`)
--   hf*           an area that ticks around the hit robot and follows it (Override), leaving it out
--   link, share   chained robots share `share` of the damage any one of them takes for `link` s
--   decoy         a fake hero the robots chase for `decoy` s (`decoyAt` = "origin" leaves it where you were)
--   drop*         a burst `dropDelay` s later where the cast landed (or where the hero stood)
--   allyBuff      heroes inside a field get this buff (`allyBuffValue`) each tick; allyHeal heals them
--   selfBuff      the cast also buffs the hero (`selfValue`, `selfDur`); "hidden" makes robots lose you
--   curve         a bolt that ignores cover; through: a dash that breaks the buildings it passes
-- All moves are original (genre ideas only, nothing named or shaped after a real show).

